+/*
+ * Two payloads that carry a NUMBER rather than a class (D-060). The class
+ * values above are all < 8, so the top two bits are free to say "this tag is a
+ * number, and here is which one".
+ *
+ *   0x8000 | d : the VIEW DEPTH, in PD units, of the next 2D rectangle. PD
+ *                draws its light glares as screen-space texture rectangles at
+ *                a position it projected itself (artifact.c), so they have no
+ *                matrix and therefore no disparity - they sit ON the panel
+ *                while the fixture they belong to sits at its own depth, which
+ *                is what the user reported as "every time i look at a light, it
+ *                hurts". The tag is consumed by ONE rectangle and hands the
+ *                renderer the depth it needs to shift that rectangle per eye.
+ *
+ *   0x4000 | s : bgGetScaleBg2Gfx() x 1024, STICKY for the rest of the frame.
+ *                The rooms are drawn in a view space scaled by this (player.c
+ *                mtx00015f04(scale, &sp8c)), so an eye offset expressed in
+ *                view units means a different PHYSICAL separation for the room
+ *                than for the body standing in it. Half on Villa, Crash Site
+ *                and Air Base, and anything at all while a scope is zoomed.
